# Labels ARE committed, deliberately: they are the expensive artifact (~$10 of
# API spend), they carry no abstracts, and they compress to a fraction of their
# size. Anyone can re-run aggregate.py and reproduce every published number
# without paying to re-label. Raw papers stay local - those are the big files.
